 that it is something positive and less than 0.37. Here we are relying on the completeness property of the real numbers, discussed in Appendix 6."},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.76249,"w":0.54393,"h":0.01518,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The comparison of e-x2 and e-x in Example 6 is a special case of the following test."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.79928,"w":0.52758,"h":0.03858,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"THEOREM 2—Direct Comparison Test Let ƒ and g be continuous on 3a, q) with 0 … ƒ(x) … g(x) for all x Ú a. Then"},{"x":0.40342,"y":0.86342,"w":0.15619,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"ƒ(x)dx converges if"},{"x":0.62126,"y":0.86342,"w":0.14708,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"g(x)dx converges."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.86437,"w":0.03642,"h":0.02268,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"1. L"},{"x":0.40342,"y":0.90946,"w":0.1453,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"g(x)dx diverges if"},{"x":0.61037,"y":0.90946,"w":0.13539,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"ƒ(x)dx diverges."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.91041,"w":0.03642,"h":0.02268,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2. L"}]}